annotated-verses.txt
--------------------

one line per verse
  tagged with all personal subjects and objects of all verbs

each verb is a scene
  who is present in the scene - frames
    - narrator/author always present
    - subject, object, others also present
    - not present but referred to
      - by narrator
      - by character
    - can recurse when narrator/character quotes a prophet
      - prophet becomes narrator/author

      dialogue
      prophecy
      dialogue + prophecy

- first reading - justa
- second reading - by English section
- third reading - by English verse
- fourth reading - SBLGNT - by verb

taxonomy
  nature - sea stones bread wheat chaff dove ... a lot of this, some as character
  peoples ~= places - bethlehem judaea jerusalem israel east
  multitude - as multitude
  group - scribes chief-priests pharisees
  small-group - wise-men shepherds
  anon - 
  named - 
